  "content": {
    "id": "p99-q41-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "41",
    "prompt": "Bob and Mary can complete a project together in 12 days. Working alone, Bob takes 10 days longer than Mary to complete the same project. In how many days will Bob complete the project by himself?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p99-q41-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "30 days.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p99-q41-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add the daily rates and solve ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{b-10}=\\frac{1}{12}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", where ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "b>10",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " is Bob’s time in days.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let Bob take $b$ days. Mary takes $b-10$ days, so $b>10$.\n\nAssuming constant, independent rates, Bob and Mary complete $\\frac{1}{b}$ and $\\frac{1}{b-10}$ of the project per day. Their combined rate is $\\frac{1}{12}$ of the project per day.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{b-10}&=\\frac{1}{12}\\end{align*}$$\n\nMultiply both sides by the nonzero common denominator $12b(b-10)$, then rearrange and factor.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}12(b-10)+12b&=b(b-10)\\\\b^2-34b+120&=0\\\\(b-30)(b-4)&=0\\\\b&=30\\text{ or }b=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $b=4$ because $b>10$. Bob takes $30$ days.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
